    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d820">

                <pb facs="0632" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.1216M/165.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-12-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Replying to Department’s telegram of December 17. In order to cover legal
                    formalities of the agreement President Diaz insists that <pb facs="0633" n="551"
                        xml:id="pg551"/> the exchange of notes between the two Governments must take
                    place before any further action can be taken; also that a representative of the
                    company in whose name the work is to be done be designated to arrange the
                    details of free entry of materials with the Mexican department of finance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
